# DATA GOVERNANCE GUARDIAN: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

## 1. DELETE PROHIBITION — No Hard Deletes
Never write `doc.delete()` or `.remove()` on a Firestore document unless inside `TrashService`:
```typescript
// ❌ FORBIDDEN — permanent data loss
await db.collection('users').doc(uid).delete();

// ✅ REQUIRED — soft delete with audit trail
await db.collection('users').doc(uid).update({
  'metadata.isDeleted': true,
  'metadata.deletedAt': FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),
  'metadata.deletedBy': adminUid,
});
```
All `findAll` / `list` queries MUST implicitly filter: `.where('metadata.isDeleted', '==', false)`.

## 2. DUAL ADMIN PROTOCOL (Hard Delete Path)
When a record must be permanently deleted (GDPR erasure):
1. Requires TWO admin tokens — initiating admin + confirming admin.
2. Logged to immutable `audit_log` collection before execution.
3. All downstream `Storage` objects (avatars, files) purged in the same transaction.
4. GDPR deletion confirmed via email to requestor within 30 days.

## 3. FIRESTORE SECURITY RULES — Delete Lockdown
```javascript
// ✅ Firestore rules — block client-side delete entirely
match /users/{userId} {
  allow delete: if false; // NEVER allow client delete
  allow update: if request.auth.token.admin == true
    || request.resource.data.metadata.isDeleted == resource.data.metadata.isDeleted; // Only admins can flip isDeleted
}
```

## 4. BACKUP & PITR
- **Point-in-Time Recovery**: Enable PITR on all Firestore databases. Retention: 7 days minimum.
- **Export Schedule**: Daily Firestore export to GCS bucket `gs://[project]-firestore-backups/`.
- **Verify**: Monthly restoration drill — restore to staging, confirm data integrity.

## 5. SCHEMA EVOLUTION
- Never rename an existing Firestore field directly — add new field, migrate data, deprecate old.
- All schema changes documented in `MISSION_STATE.md` under `## Schema Migrations`.
